va runtime reports (`-XshowSettings:properties` or the `java.version` TLC prints) and\n      record it in the report and in the environment digest.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-09T160748\n    date: \"2026-10-09\"\n    title: \"The TLC result says exhaustive and check-formal prints an exhaustive search for a run interrupted at its budget\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: adapters\n    what_happened: >\n      `TlcResult.exhaustive` (`src/adapters/formal/tlc.ts`) is true as soon as TLC announces its breadth-first mode\n      (message 2187), and its comment reads \"Whether TLC ran the breadth-first search of the whole state space\". On\n      the incident witness, stopped by its 3 s budget, the result is `inconclusive` with `exhaustive: true`, and\n      `check-formal` prints `search: exhaustive breadth-first; states: unknown`. The outcome, `pass: false` and the\n      exit code 2 stay right; the field and the line describe the mode asked for, not an exploration that covered\n      the state space.\n    what_expected: >\n      The field and the printed line say the search mode TLC was asked to run, and never read as a search of the\n      whole state space when the exploration did not finish.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"Run `node scripts/check-formal.ts specs/formal/fixtures/tlc/incident/manifest.json --jar <tla2tools.jar>`: `inconclusive`, exit 2, and the line `search: exhaustive breadth-first`.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      `exhaustive` is computed from the mode message alone, and its name and comment speak of the whole state space.\n    evidence: >\n      Introduced by the branch e38s02, which adds the TLC reader. Noted by its acceptance run; confirmed at the\n      arbitration on the incident witness and its raw output, which holds message 2187 and neither 2193 nor 2186.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Rename the field to the mode (`mode: \"breadth-first\" | \"depth-first\" | \"simulation\"`) or print\n      `breadth-first, not finished` when the outcome is not `completed`.\n    status: open\nEOF\nnode -e 'const y=require(require.resolve(\"yaml\",{paths:[require(\"child_process\").execSync(\"npm root -g\").toString().trim()+\"/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\"]}));const d=y.parse(require(\"fs\").readFileSync(\"specs/bugs/registry.yaml\",\"utf8\"));console.log(d.bugs.length,d.bugs.at(-1).bug_id)' 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Append two registry entries and parse YAML"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":408,"cache_read_input_tokens":60406,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":408},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c7f243d9-e09b-4148-953d-b0c27808e0e2","uuid":"a4190ac3-3a93-43c8-b4fd-73286a3899fa","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:08:01.552Z","request_id":"req_011Cfro16611GtmYLBLK3u1e","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VFeVpx5ZDP9ubvfx5b1yfa":{"command":"cd /Users/jeanjerome/Projets/495-pi-package && cat >> specs/bugs/registry.yaml <<'EOF'\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-09T160747\n    date: \"2026-10-09\"\n    title: \"The check-formal report names the Java runtime by its command only, without its version\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: scripts\n    what_happened: >\n      `check-formal` (`scripts/check-formal.ts`) records in its report `tool.java` as the command it was given\n      (`java` by default) and identifies the environment of the evidence by `digestValue({ java: options.java })`.\n      The version and the digest of TLC's jar are recorded, the version of the Java runtime that ran it is not: two\n      runs under two different JVMs carry the same report fields and the same environment digest. The fixtures README\n      declares the Java measured on the refe